sieve-filter-v2
; melody-lengths-v2 for the notes3 family: note and rest lengths from shortest to longest (length
; codes, as that many sixteenths of TPQ ticks), and at most so many of an eighth or shorter in a
; row. The state is how many short ones have come in a row.
id        melody-lengths-notes3
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     audio
symbols   notes3*
describe  Note lengths from shortest to longest, and at most so many eighths (or shorter) in a row.
param     shortest  choice  s s,e,E,q,Q,h,H,w the shortest note or rest allowed
param     longest   choice  w s,e,E,q,Q,h,H,w the longest note or rest allowed
param     eighths   int     2  0  32  the most notes or rests of an eighth or shorter in a row

states    {eighths + 1}
start     0
accept    0..{eighths}
for s 0 {eighths}
  for n 1 {LONGEST}
    if {n * 4 >= SIXTEENTHS(shortest) * TPQ && n * 4 <= SIXTEENTHS(longest) * TPQ}
      if {n * 2 <= TPQ}
        if {s < eighths}
          t {s} @{REST(n)} {s + 1}
          for p 1 {PITCHES}
            for k 1 {LEVELS}
              t {s} @{NOTE(p, k, n)} {s + 1}
            done
          done
        fi
      else
        t {s} @{REST(n)} 0
        for p 1 {PITCHES}
          for k 1 {LEVELS}
            t {s} @{NOTE(p, k, n)} 0
          done
        done
      fi
    fi
  done
done
end
